[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded requested deck option and directive profiles

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-OPTIONS-DEFAULTTEMP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit fixed operating temperature
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated preparation shall accept root .OPTION or .OPTIONS TEMP=27 and root .TEMP 27 with a literal Celsius value numerically equal to 27. A temperature option may share a card with individually admitted reporting settings. The adapter shall retain the source range and leave the fixed 300.15 K model contract in effect. The original temperature card shall remain present in the native oracle input. Other temperatures, unsupported expressions, temperature lists and unsupported co-options shall refuse explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: DeclarationExtraction, OperatingPointSelection, and OriginalProjection. Verification: AccountingOptionTests and original requested corpus replay. The engine does not expose a general operating temperature, nominal temperature or native device convergence policy through this profile.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-SELECT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REPORT-WIDTH-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded legacy reporting width
STATEMENT: >>>
Explicit selection may omit a root .WIDTH card consisting of one or both of IN and OUT with positive integer literal values, each key at most once. The omission shall retain the original source range. Other width forms shall remain explicit refusals. Strict lowering shall remain unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ngspice src/frontend/inp.c takes .WIDTH out of the physical input. src/frontend/dotcards.c applies output width to reporting. Verification: AccountingOptionTests and original requested corpus replay.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-SELECT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-DIODE-ZERO-RS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit zero diode series resistance
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated diode profile shall admit an RS value that evaluates to zero with unchanged topology and charge parameters. Positive values follow SEMI-DIODE-SERIES-R-001. Duplicate and invalid values shall refuse. Circuit readiness and physical preparation shall use the same admissibility rule. The independent ngspice comparison shall retain the original model card.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: SemiconductorPreparation. Verification: DirectiveFollowupTests and the original qualification-diode-constant-charge.cir replay.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CSPARAM-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded scalar control constant exports
STATEMENT: >>>
A root .CSPARAM assignment with a simple name shall evaluate one finite scalar from the deck parameter environment and export it only to the bounded control reporting namespace. The export shall be available before and after dispatch. Preserve the original card in the native oracle. Refuse invalid or duplicate exports, names reserved by the native constant plot or analysis axes, and writes to an exported constant. Nested or opaque exports shall remain explicit refusals.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: DeclarationExtraction, RequestedControlConstants, and ControlVectorExecution. Native reference: ngspice frontend inp.c const-plot initialization and cpitf.c built-in constants. Verification: RequestedOptionConstantTests, original corpus replay and separate native scalar export fixture. Control loops, model edits and conditional netlist semantics are outside this requirement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-TRAN-ABSTOL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Absolute current convergence tolerance for requested transient
STATEMENT: >>>
A transient-only requested program may specify one root .opt, .option or .options ABSTOL assignment. The frontend shall evaluate it to a finite positive tolerance in amperes and carry it to nonlinear time-zero bias and transient Newton solves, including adaptive trial solves. Linear solves and timestep error control shall retain their existing policies. Unrecognized companion options, duplicate ABSTOL assignments and mixed-analysis programs shall refuse. A missing assignment shall retain the existing default.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: DeclarationExtraction, RequestedAnalysis, the typed client transient configuration and configured.rs. TransientAbstolTests verifies the serialized value and refuses invalid or unsupported options. Managed verification recorded 21 passes and four environment-gated skips. Removing the frontend assignment failed the targeted regression, which passed after restoration. Scoped Coverlet line/branch results were 74.24/55.06 percent for DeclarationExtraction and 53.55/35.29 percent for RequestedAnalysis.cs. Native execution and coverage remain pending because available RAM was below the guarded native build admission threshold. The original mosmem.cir requested path advances to unsupported_pulse_overlap. Artifacts: E:/Artifacts/Spice-abstol-52caf35.
<<<
